# wfg-log 1
# fixture lane-record - a cue's lanes recorded from the faders: the flip, a REC,
# the refusals, and a pass (namespace draft §20.9, and §34 since 2026-10-06).
#
# WHAT IT IS FOR: that the lane commands and every refusal they owe reproduce
# exactly under both locales. Recorded from a real `wfg serve` of
# tests/fixtures/bundles/lane-record driven over OSC with NO audio device -
# which is why the pass below ends with nothing written: with no sample clock
# there is no second of the file for a hand to be recorded at. The lanes a pass
# writes are an engine `lane.write` in the log of a session that had sound, and
# `blackbox/lane_record.py` replays one of those every run. The header lines
# below are the session's own.
#
# EDITED BY HAND ON 2026-10-06, when §34 flipped the faders: the touch that took
# one fader (`lane.take`, DF) became a strip's REC (`lane.rec`), and §20.9's
# `not-waiting` and `no-fader` became `not-flipped`. Every other record is the
# session's.
#
# bundle lane-record sha256:45c4cb58b8d985e45c412c4941869f5a85caf3e5ee342541aa7a67951ebf1efe
# clock sampleRate=48000 blockSize=128 samplesPerTick=960
# media tone.wav 0 0.000
#
# NOTHING IS FLIPPED, so a REC arms nothing and there is no pass: both are
# `not-flipped`; and a list is not a media cue.
R 26 0 udp:127.0.0.1:54584 not-flipped lane.rec s:"level" T
R 41 1 udp:127.0.0.1:54586 not-flipped lane.record
R 56 2 udp:127.0.0.1:54587 bad-value lane.arm s:"VR000001"
#
# THE FLIP (UI): the faders show the cue, and the level's REC arms its lane - a
# lane the faders do not show refused.
A 71 3 udp:127.0.0.1:54588 lane.arm s:"VR000002"
A 86 4 udp:127.0.0.1:54589 lane.rec s:"level" T
R 101 5 udp:127.0.0.1:54590 bad-value lane.rec s:"VR000007" T
#
# A HAND SETTING THE FADER BEFORE ANY PASS: applied through the live door, and
# ignored - nothing is written until a touch in a pass (DG).
A 116 6 udp:127.0.0.1:54591 node.set s:"/godot/surface/laneRide" f:-3
#
# THE PASS: the cue fired as `cue.fire` fires it, the run's drawn identifier in
# the record; the faders cannot be flipped back under it.
A 131 7 udp:127.0.0.1:54592 lane.record d:0 s:"Y63KSHEK"
R 146 8 udp:127.0.0.1:54593 busy lane.free
#
# The ride: touched, set, let go - latched - and the hand's stop.
A 161 9 udp:127.0.0.1:54594 node.touch s:"/godot/surface/laneRide"
A 176 10 udp:127.0.0.1:54595 node.set s:"/godot/surface/laneRide" f:-9
A 191 11 udp:127.0.0.1:54596 node.release s:"/godot/surface/laneRide"
A 206 12 udp:127.0.0.1:54597 lane.stop
#
# THE RUNNER ENDS IT on the next tick: the cue stopped, and the pass cleared as
# kept - with no lane written, there being no sound to have been at a second of.
# (Recorded before K4 and §30.4: a session today logs `run.stop` here, and
# `lane.stop s:"untouched"`, a pass with nothing to write. The handlers take
# these records as they took them then, and since §34 the faders stay flipped
# after a pass - UM.)
A 207 13 engine run.kill s:"Y63KSHEK"
A 207 14 engine lane.stop s:"kept"
A 208 15 engine run.ended s:"Y63KSHEK"
#
# And `lane.free`, applied: the faders flip back.
A 246 16 udp:127.0.0.1:54598 lane.free
